Z||000000||batboy||09-18-1999||11:48 AM||||Every year the SCCA Solo II Nationals race right next "door" to where I work in Topeka, Kansas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> This year I met a nice couple from Nevada that have a fully race-prepped IMSA GTU Fiero that they both run in one of the modified classes. For pics and more info go to my webpage at:  <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||09-20-1999||09:05 AM||||Hey, Batboy, that's really cool!  I love road racing, so naturally I love the GTU Fieros.  Incidentally, there are usually one or two of these in the GT-2 class at the SCCA Nationals every year.  The Nationals are in three weeks, so I'll take my camera and hope some Fieros show up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||09-20-1999||10:23 PM||||Chad, please do take your camera. I'd like to see other pics of these neat race Fieros. You ought to try to get an action shot. I failed to do that, becaused they already raced before I arrived.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||09-20-1999||11:28 PM||||batboy...<BR>This nice couple from Nevada?<BR>did you happen to catch where from nevada?<BR>I am here in vegas, and if they are in my neck of the desert, I may have the possibility of stumbling across this nice couple, and taking a peek at it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||09-21-1999||07:35 AM||||Their names are Rick and Barbara, but didn't catch their last name. They told me what town the live by, but I don't remember. About an hour drive north of Las Vegas I think. They race in the Las Vegas area SCCA region.||||reg||1
